13. The troubleshooting logic Elias will probably follow
This is the part I’d understand rather than just memorizing commands.

Step 1 — Is the AP configured correctly?
show ap config general WAPGOZ92_24
Primary should be ADC.

Step 2 — Can AP reach primary WLC?
From AP:
ping 172.28.182.214
If no → network/routing path.
If yes → continue.

Step 3 — Start debugs on ADC.
debug mac addr <AP-radio-MAC>
debug capwap events enable
debug capwap errors enable
debug dtls all enable

Step 4 — Start AP debugs.
debug capwap client event
debug capwap client error
debug dtls client event
debug dtls client error
term mon

Step 5 — Reset ONE AP from CNJ.
config ap reset WAPGOZ92_24

Step 6 — Observe.

There are basically four outcomes:
AP never contacts ADC → discovery/reachability issue.
ADC receives discovery but rejects AP → controller config/AP authorization/certificate/etc.
CAPWAP establishes but DTLS fails → certificate/DTLS issue.
AP successfully joins ADC → failback works; schedule controlled migration of remaining ADC APs after the approved window.

Then immediately:
debug disable-all

and on AP:
undebug all
That one-AP controlled test is what I’d push to accomplish on today’s TAC session before anyone considers moving hundreds of APs. 




















